2. Can we do host header injection on the login page?

Ans: 
Yes, we can test for Host Header Injection on a login page. 
I would modify the Host header and observe whether the application uses that value in redirects, password reset links, or generated URLs.
If the application trusts the user-supplied Host header, it could be vulnerable.

Example
User requests a password reset. Attacker modifies the Host header to evil.com.
Application generates:   https://evil.com/reset?token=abc123
User clicks the link from the email.  The attacker captures the reset token and may take over the account.

